# Agentic / implementation routing

**ADF status mirror: COMPLETE ADF-A–ADF-H; ADF-EX-17 DEFERRED VERIFICATION; FOUNDATION EXIT ACCEPTED.**

**CKR status mirror: COMPLETE CKR-A–CKR-K; CKR EXIT ACCEPTED.**

**DPTN status mirror: COMPLETE DPTN-A; NEXT DPTN-B; IMPLEMENTATION 001-A BLOCKED ON DPTN EXIT.**

ADF and CKR are complete/accepted. DPTN-A is complete/accepted; DPTN-B is NEXT / READY / NOT STARTED. Implementation 001-A is BLOCKED / NOT STARTED until DPTN-G exit acceptance and a later explicit human-selected implementation task.

Primary shared authority remains root `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agentic_development_foundation/authority_scope_policy.md`, the CKR ownership inventory, accepted ADF scope/security mechanics, and the live DPTN authority for topology changes only.

For a known stable ID, use `python3 scripts/agentic/resolve_stable_id.py <ID>` to get the **current** canonical locator. Use `--history` only for explicit provenance/history. For an unknown semantic location, use one bounded route from `knowledge/index.md`, then the current canonical owner.

DPTN-A accepted destinations in `docs/documentation_topology_normalization/move_map.json` remain planning only. Do not route current semantic work to those paths. DPTN-B physical relocation begins only after explicit human selection of DPTN-B.

Do not begin Implementation 001-A while DPTN is active. Do not infer authority from the DPTN move map, OKF, resolver output alone, recency, search order, Git history, vendor skill, tool memory, source availability or path presence.
